{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who is the man who is fearful, etc.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 44a): this refers to one who fears the transgressions in his hand — meaning, along the lines of the verse (Isaiah 33:14): ״פָּחֲדוּ בְצִיּוֹן חַטָּאִים״, for anyone who has transgressions in his hand, his heart is fearful and trembles of itself; and even if he does not know that he has transgressions, the fear that enters his heart in battle will inform him that he has transgressions. And our Sages of blessed memory (Orach Chayim, sec. 54, citing the Yerushalmi) gauged the sin by the fear that enters a person's heart from his Maker — that even if he has done nothing more than speak between Yishtabach and Yozer. And the reason is that one who enters battle needs a miracle to be saved from the enemy's sword, and anyone who has in him any aspect of evil is not worthy of a miracle, and his fortune will frighten him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:11.914434233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}